! An oxygen chain with a spin spiral along it, on an ultrasoft dataset -- the
! system the augmented spiral is validated on.
!
! It is the hydrogen chain of h-chain-spiral.in with the one change that matters:
! the dataset carries an augmentation charge, so the transverse block of the
! density is built from the *displaced* table Q_ij(G - q) rather than from
! Q_ij(G). One oxygen per cell, 5.2 bohr apart along z and 12 bohr from its
! images in x and y, with the moment turned into the plane (angle1 = 90) so the
! whole moment sits in the transverse channel the displacement governs -- a
! moment along z would leave that channel empty and the test would pass on a
! quantity that is zero.
!
! Three choices are deliberate and the identities depend on all three:
!
!   * celldm(3) = 0.43333... puts the chain spacing at 5.2 bohr, which is the
!     one nearby value whose FFT grids *double and quadruple exactly*: dense
!     24 -> 48 -> 96 and smooth 18 -> 36 -> 72. At 5.0 bohr the doubled cell
!     takes 45 dense points rather than 48, and the two cells then discretise
!     the same functional differently -- worth 4.9e-06 Ry, which is larger than
!     the identity being tested.
!   * degauss = 0.1, for the reason h-chain-spiral.in gives: a soft magnetic
!     surface at a small smearing lands the spiral and its supercell in
!     different minima.
!   * the 1x1x4 k-grid is even, so it is invariant under a shift by half a
!     reciprocal lattice vector.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 0.43333333333333,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0, ecutrho = 200.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.10
    noncolin = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6
    angle1(1) = 90.0
    spiral_q(1) = 0.0, spiral_q(2) = 0.0, spiral_q(3) = 0.25
    nbnd = 10
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 O  16.0  O.pz-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 O 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 4 0 0 0
